  - sovereign cloud
  - cloud repatriation
  - aws alternative
  - windows server
  - hyper v
  - service fabric
  - gitops
  - zero trust
  - architecture decision records
abstract: >
  Argus is a design record for moving a mid-sized organisation's AWS
  workloads onto Windows Server hardware it owns: thirty-five architecture
  decisions, an application infrastructure map, a hardware-rooted security
  architecture and a phased plan. The platform itself is not built. A console
  prototype, a read-only console API and a Docker Compose stack of the
  open-source components run and are tested.
